window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-171fdaa74f75310f"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"remote-connections\">远程连接（Remote connections）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档目录见 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面的 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>远程连接可让你访问在另一台设备或计算机上运行的工作内容。在 iOS 版 ChatGPT 移动应用中，打开 <strong>Codex</strong>，即可在已连接的 Mac 或 Windows 设备上处理 ChatGPT 或 Codex 对话。如果你的移动应用仍显示 <strong>Remote</strong>，请改为打开该入口。你也可以从另一台受支持的设备上的 ChatGPT 桌面应用继续工作，或将应用连接到 SSH 主机上的项目。</p> <p>远程访问使用已连接主机上的项目、对话、文件、凭据、权限、插件、Computer Use（计算机操作）、浏览器设置和本地工具。</p> <p><span id=\"local-computer-access-and-remote-connections\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"local-computer-access-with-work-cloud-and-remote-connections\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"work-cloud\">使用 Work Cloud 和远程连接访问本机计算机</h2> <p>如果你的工作区启用了 Work Cloud 本机计算机访问功能，符合条件的 ChatGPT Work 对话可以在桌面、移动设备和网页之间继续。OpenAI 云端负责协调任务；已联网并连接的计算机则可以执行需要使用其本地资源的步骤。</p> <p>对于使用此功能的对话，请参阅 Work Cloud 本机计算机访问指南。下文关于远程访问和 SSH 的说明适用于现有受支持的主机连接工作流。查看此功能下的对话所需的设置，可能与 Codex 主机连接所需的设置不同。</p> <p>Work Cloud 本机计算机访问只适用于启用同步之后创建的任务。原有任务（包括项目中的任务）仍保持原来的模式：仅在本机运行，或在云端运行但无法访问本地文件。要使用此功能，请新建一个任务。</p> <p>如果某个新轮次开始时计算机不可用，正在使用 Work Cloud 本机计算机访问的符合条件任务可以继续在云容器中运行。云容器无法访问不可用计算机上的文件或工具，也不会强制执行仅适用于本机执行的企业要求。任务不能在某一轮进行期间从本机执行切换到云端。此功能不会改变 Codex 移动版连接主机的方式。</p> <p><a id=\"what-you-can-do-remotely\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">你可以远程执行哪些操作</h2> <ul> <li>在主机上的项目中新建对话，或继续已有对话。</li> <li>发送后续指令、回答问题并引导正在进行的工作。</li> <li>批准命令及其他操作。</li> <li>查看输出、差异、测试结果、终端输出和屏幕截图。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT 完成任务或需要你关注时接收通知。</li> <li>在已连接的主机和对话之间切换。</li> </ul> <p>接下来的部分介绍如何使用 ChatGPT 移动应用访问桌面主机。若要将 Codex 连接到 SSH 主机上的项目，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=connect-to-an-ssh-host\">连接到 SSH 主机</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 移动应用中的移动设备连接设置界面</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-set-up-remote\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"before-you-set-up-mobile-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">设置移动访问之前</h2> <p>远程访问支持运行 ChatGPT 桌面应用的 macOS 和 Windows 主机。你可以通过 iOS 或 Android 版 ChatGPT 控制主机；如果 <strong>Control other devices（控制其他设备）</strong> 功能已向你开放，也可以通过另一台 Mac 或 Windows 设备控制。功能可用范围可能会随逐步开放而变化。</p> <p>请确认你具备以下条件：</p> <ul> <li>你想使用的 ChatGPT 账号和工作区都允许访问 Codex。</li> <li>iOS 或 Android 设备上安装了最新版 ChatGPT 移动应用。如果 iOS 应用中看不到 <strong>Codex</strong>，或使用旧版界面的应用中看不到 <strong>Remote</strong>，请先更新 ChatGPT。</li> <li>主机上运行着最新版 macOS 或 Windows 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用；主机必须处于唤醒状态、已联网，并登录同一账号和工作区。移动访问必须从应用中设置，不能通过 Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展进行设置。</li> <li>该账号或工作区要求的多重身份验证、SSO 或通行密钥配置。</li> </ul> <p>如果你通过 ChatGPT 工作区使用 Codex，管理员可能需要先启用 Remote Control（远程控制）访问权限，你才能从手机连接。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-remote\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"set-up-mobile-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">设置移动访问</h2> <p>请在要连接的主机上的 ChatGPT 桌面应用中开始设置。设置流程会为该主机启用远程访问，然后显示一个二维码，供你用手机扫描。 该二维码会将手机与主机配对。每台你想用来控制主机的手机或受支持的桌面应用设备，都要与相应主机配对。</p> <p>自 2026 年 6 月 8 日以来使用过的现有连接仍保持配对。如果自 2026 年 6 月 8 日以来没有使用过某个现有连接，请更新两端的应用并重新配对设备。</p> <ol> <li>在计算机上开始设置。</li> </ol> <p>在主机上打开 ChatGPT 桌面应用。前往 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> &gt; <strong>Connections（连接）</strong> &gt; <strong>Control this Mac or PC（控制这台 Mac 或 PC）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Set up（设置）</strong> 或 <strong>Add（添加）</strong>。批准远程访问，并完成应用要求的验证。</p> <ol> <li>扫描二维码。</li> </ol> <p>使用手机扫描应用显示的二维码。该二维码会打开 ChatGPT，让你完成移动应用与主机的连接。</p> <ol> <li>在 ChatGPT 中完成设置。</li> </ol> <p>ChatGPT 会打开连接设置流程。确认使用的是同一个 ChatGPT 账号和工作区，然后完成所需的多重身份验证、SSO 或通行密钥步骤。设置成功后，主机就会显示在 iOS 版 <strong>Codex</strong> 中；如果你的移动应用仍使用旧名称，则会显示在 <strong>Remote</strong> 中。</p> <ol> <li>检查主机设置。</li> </ol> <p>在主机上的应用中，前往 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> &gt; <strong>Connections（连接）</strong> 管理已连接设备。你还可以选择是否让计算机保持唤醒、启用 Computer Use（计算机操作），或安装 Chrome 扩展程序。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Connections（连接）控件，用于允许设备控制此 Mac 并让它保持唤醒</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"choose-what-to-connect\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">选择要连接的设备或环境</h2> <p>先从你平时使用 ChatGPT 的笔记本电脑或台式电脑开始。如果需要持续访问，或需要使用不同的环境，再添加一台常开计算机或 SSH 主机。</p> <h3 id=\"_5\"></h3>  <p>你的笔记本电脑或台式电脑</p> <p>连接已安装桌面应用的 Mac 或 Windows 电脑。远程访问就能使用你当前使用的相同项目、对话、凭据、插件和本地设置。</p> <p>如果计算机进入睡眠、断网或关闭应用，远程访问就会停止，直到该计算机重新可用。如果将这台计算机用作主机，请保持连接电源，并在可用时通过主机的连接设置让它保持唤醒。</p> <p>在 Mac 笔记本电脑上，打开上盖并连接电源时，远程访问可以保持可用。合上上盖时，还需连接外接显示器。选择 <strong>Sleep（睡眠）</strong> 仍会停止远程访问。</p> <p>在 Windows 主机上，如果任务会使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a>，请保持会话处于解锁和可用状态。Windows 上的 Computer Use 会在前台运行，因此远程控制更适合用于启动或检查工作；执行任务期间，主机桌面应留给该任务使用。</p> <h3 id=\"_6\"></h3>  <p>专用常开计算机</p> <p>如果你希望 ChatGPT 在较长时间内都能连接到主机，可以使用专用的常开 Mac 或 Windows 电脑。</p> <p>请在这台计算机上安装 ChatGPT 或 Codex 需要使用的项目、凭据、MCP 服务器、Skills 和工具。</p> <h3 id=\"_7\"></h3>  <p>远程开发环境</p> <p>如果项目已经位于远程环境中，可以使用 SSH 主机或托管的远程开发环境。先将桌面应用所在的主机连接到该环境；你的手机仍连接同一台主机，而 ChatGPT 会在远程环境中工作，并使用该环境的依赖项、安全策略和计算资源。</p> <p>有关 SSH 设置详情，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=connect-to-an-ssh-host\">连接到 SSH 主机</a>。</p> <p>如果要在常开计算机或远程主机上执行浏览器或桌面任务，请启用 Computer Use，并在该主机上安装 Chrome 扩展程序。</p> <p><a id=\"what-comes-from-the-connected-host\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">哪些资源来自已连接主机</h2> <p>手机会将提示词、审批和后续消息发送给 ChatGPT；已连接主机则提供 ChatGPT 使用的运行环境。</p> <p>也就是说：</p> <ul> <li>仓库文件和本地文档来自已连接主机。</li> <li>Shell 命令会在该主机或远程环境上运行。</li> <li>MCP 服务器、Skills、浏览器访问和 Computer Use 均来自该主机的配置。</li> <li>只有在主机能够访问的情况下，ChatGPT 才能使用已登录的网站和桌面应用。</li> <li>连接会话仍受沙盒设置、安全控制和操作审批规则约束。</li> </ul> <p>安全中继层可让已获授权的 ChatGPT 设备访问受信任计算机，而无需将这些计算机直接暴露到公共互联网。</p> <p><a id=\"pick-up-work-from-another-device\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">从另一台设备继续工作</h2> <p>你可以在另一台已登录且支持远程控制的 ChatGPT 桌面应用设备上继续工作。例如，如果笔记本电脑暂时不可用，你可以先在手机上通过一台常开主机启动对话，之后再打开笔记本电脑上的应用，继续同一个对话。</p> <p>在功能可用的 Mac 或 Windows 设备上，前往 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Connections（连接）&gt; Control other devices（控制其他设备）</strong>，添加另一台主机。一台设备可以同时允许远程访问，并控制另一台设备。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Connections（连接）设置卡片，用于通过此 Mac 控制另一台设备</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"connect-to-an-ssh-host\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"ssh\">连接到 SSH 主机</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中添加 SSH 主机上的远程项目，即可针对远程文件系统和 Shell 运行对话。远程项目对话会在远程主机上执行命令、读取文件并写入更改。</p> <p>请让远程主机遵循你对普通 SSH 访问所采用的安全要求：使用受信任的密钥、遵循最小权限原则，并且不要开放未经身份验证的公共监听端口。</p> <ol> <li>在 SSH 配置中添加主机，让 Codex 可以自动发现它。</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Host devbox\n     HostName devbox.example.com\n     User you\n     IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519\n</code></pre> <p>Codex 会从 <code>~/.ssh/config</code> 中读取具体的主机别名，通过 OpenSSH 解析它们，并忽略只有模式、没有具体主机名的条目。</p> <ol> <li>确认可以从运行应用的计算机通过 SSH 连接到该主机。</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   ssh devbox\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>在远程主机上安装 Codex，并完成身份验证。</li> </ol> <p>应用会通过 SSH，以远程用户的登录 Shell 启动远程 Codex app server。请确认在该 Shell 中，<code>codex</code> 命令可以从 <code>PATH</code> 找到。</p> <ol> <li>在应用中打开 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Connections（连接）</strong>，添加或启用 SSH 主机，然后选择远程项目文件夹。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>插图：Connections（连接）SSH 列表，显示三台远程主机</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"hand-off-a-thread-between-hosts\"></a> <a id=\"hand-off-a-chat-between-hosts\"></a> <a id=\"hand-off-a-task-between-hosts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">在主机之间移交对话</h2> <p>移交（Handoff）会在本地计算机与已连接的远程主机之间迁移现有对话及其 Git 状态。你可以先在本机开始工作，再到远程计算机的工作树中继续，之后还可以把对话带回本机。</p> <p>移交对话之前，请连接目标主机，并在该主机上为同一个 Git 仓库保存项目。如果项目是仓库的子目录，请在两台主机上保存相同的子目录。Codex 只会显示具有匹配已保存项目的目标位置。</p> <p>移交对话的步骤：</p> <ol> <li>在桌面应用中打开该对话。</li> <li>在对话页脚中选择当前运行位置，再选择目标主机。将远程对话交还本机时，请选择 <strong>This computer（本机）</strong>。</li> <li>检查目标位置和分支，然后选择 <strong>Hand off（移交）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>Codex 会在目标主机上创建或复用一个工作树，传输对话及 Git 状态，并将该对话切换到目标主机。如果对话正在运行，移交前会中断当前回复。</p> <p>你也可以在另一个对话中要求 Codex 将指定对话移交到已连接的主机。Codex 不能移交发出此请求的当前对话，也不支持移交到 Codex 云端环境。</p> <p><a id=\"authentication-and-network-exposure\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">身份验证与网络暴露</h2> <p>远程连接通过 SSH 启动并管理远程 Codex app server。不要将 app-server 传输端点暴露在共享网络或公共网络中。</p> <p>如果需要从当前网络之外连接远程计算机，请使用 VPN 或网状网络工具，而不是将 app server 直接暴露到互联网。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">故障排查</h2> <p><a id=\"you-dont-see-the-host-on-your-phone\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">手机上看不到主机</h3> <p>确认主机上的桌面应用正在运行、已启用 <strong>Allow other devices to connect（允许其他设备连接）</strong>，并且两台设备使用同一个 ChatGPT 账号和工作区。如果自 2026 年 6 月 8 日以来没有使用过该连接，请更新两端的应用并重新配对设备。</p> <p><a id=\"remote-control-is-off-after-you-sign-back-in\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"remote-control\">重新登录后 Remote Control（远程控制）已关闭</h3> <p>退出 ChatGPT 会关闭 <strong>Remote Control（远程控制）</strong>，但不会删除现有设备配对。重新登录后，打开 <strong>Remote Control（远程控制）</strong> 即可恢复此前的连接状态。</p> <p>如果打开 <strong>Remote Control（远程控制）</strong> 并选择 <strong>Add（添加）</strong> 后出现错误，请重启主机上的 ChatGPT 桌面应用，然后重试。</p> <p><a id=\"the-approval-request-doesnt-appear\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">没有出现审批请求</h3> <p>在 iOS 版 ChatGPT 移动应用中打开 <strong>Codex</strong>。如果你的移动应用仍显示 <strong>Remote</strong>，请改为打开该入口。确认手机和主机使用同一个 ChatGPT 账号和工作区，然后重新扫描二维码，或从主机重新启动设置流程。如果你使用 ChatGPT 工作区，请让管理员确认已启用 Remote Control（远程控制）访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"the-remote-session-disconnects\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_15\">远程会话断开</h3> <p>检查主机是否进入睡眠、失去网络连接或关闭了应用。ChatGPT 工作期间，请让主机保持唤醒并联网。</p> <p><a id=\"authentication-blocks-setup\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">身份验证导致设置失败</h3> <p>完成设置期间显示的账号或工作区身份验证提示。如果组织要求 SSO、多重身份验证或通行密钥，请先完成相应流程再重试。如果仍然无法设置，请让工作区管理员确认已启用 Remote Control（远程控制）访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"see-also\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_17\">另请参阅</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f449586d4612e83c\">功能</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257\">ChatGPT 桌面应用设置</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">Chrome 扩展程序</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">命令行选项</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">身份验证</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"remote-connections\">Remote connections</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Remote connections let you access work running on another device or machine. In the ChatGPT mobile app for iOS, open <strong>Codex</strong> to work with ChatGPT or Codex chats on a connected Mac or Windows device. If your mobile app still shows <strong>Remote</strong>, open it instead. You can also continue work from another supported device running the ChatGPT desktop app or connect the app to projects on an SSH host.</p> <p>Remote access uses the connected host's projects, chats, files, credentials, permissions, plugins, Computer Use, browser setup, and local tools.</p> <p><span id=\"local-computer-access-and-remote-connections\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"local-computer-access-with-work-cloud-and-remote-connections\">Local computer access with Work Cloud and Remote connections</h2> <p>When your workspace enables Local computer access with Work Cloud, eligible ChatGPT Work conversations can continue across desktop, mobile, and web. OpenAI's cloud coordinates the task, and an online, connected computer can execute steps that need its local resources.</p> <p>Use the Local computer access with Work Cloud guidance for conversations using this feature. The remote access and SSH instructions below apply to the existing supported host-connection workflows. The setup required to view a conversation using this feature may differ from the setup for a Codex host connection.</p> <p>Local computer access with Work Cloud applies only to tasks created after you enable sync. Existing tasks, including tasks in projects, keep their original mode: locally only, or in the cloud without access to local files. Start a new task to use this feature.</p> <p>If the computer is unavailable when a new turn starts, an existing eligible task using local computer access with Work Cloud can continue in a cloud container. The cloud container cannot access files or tools on the unavailable computer. It also does not enforce enterprise requirements from local execution. A task cannot switch from local execution to the cloud during a turn. This feature does not change how Codex on mobile connects to a host.</p> <h2 id=\"what-you-can-do-remotely\">What you can do remotely</h2> <ul> <li>Start new chats in projects on the host, or continue existing ones.</li> <li>Send follow-up instructions, answer questions, and steer active work.</li> <li>Approve commands and other actions.</li> <li>Review outputs, diffs, test results, terminal output, and screenshots.</li> <li>Get notified when ChatGPT completes a task or needs your attention.</li> <li>Switch between connected hosts and chats.</li> </ul> <p>The next sections cover using the ChatGPT mobile app to access a desktop host. To connect Codex to a project on an SSH host, see <a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=connect-to-an-ssh-host\">connect to an SSH host</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Mobile connection setup screen in the ChatGPT mobile app</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-set-up-remote\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"before-you-set-up-mobile-access\">Before you set up mobile access</h2> <p>Remote access supports hosts running the ChatGPT desktop app on macOS and Windows. You can control a host from ChatGPT on iOS or Android, or from another Mac or Windows device when <strong>Control other devices</strong> is available. Availability can vary by rollout.</p> <p>Make sure you have:</p> <ul> <li>Codex access in the ChatGPT account and workspace you want to use.</li> <li>The latest ChatGPT mobile app on an iOS or Android device. If you don't see <strong>Codex</strong> on iOS or <strong>Remote</strong> in an app that still uses that label, update ChatGPT first.</li> <li>The latest ChatGPT desktop app for macOS or Windows running on a host that's awake, online, and signed in to the same account and workspace. Mobile setup starts from the app; you can't set it up from the Codex CLI or IDE extension.</li> <li>Any required multi-factor authentication, SSO, or passkey configuration for that account or workspace.</li> </ul> <p>If you use Codex through a ChatGPT workspace, your admin may need to enable Remote Control access before you can connect from your phone.</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-remote\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"set-up-mobile-access\">Set up mobile access</h2> <p>Start in the ChatGPT desktop app on the host you want to connect. The setup flow enables remote access for that host, then shows a QR code you can scan from your phone. The QR code pairs that phone with that host. Pair every phone or supported desktop app device with every host you want it to control.</p> <p>Existing connections used since June 8, 2026, remain paired. If you haven't used an existing connection since June 8, 2026, update both apps and pair the devices again.</p> <ol> <li>Start setup on your computer.</li> </ol> <p>Open the ChatGPT desktop app on the host. Go to <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Connections</strong> &gt; <strong>Control this Mac or PC</strong>, then select <strong>Set up</strong> or <strong>Add</strong>. Approve remote access and complete any requested verification.</p> <ol> <li>Scan the QR code.</li> </ol> <p>Use your phone to scan the QR code shown by the app. The code opens ChatGPT so you can finish connecting the mobile app to the host.</p> <ol> <li>Finish setup in ChatGPT.</li> </ol> <p>ChatGPT opens the connection setup flow. Confirm the same ChatGPT account and workspace, then complete any required multi-factor authentication, SSO, or passkey steps. After setup succeeds, the host appears in <strong>Codex</strong> on iOS, or <strong>Remote</strong> if your mobile app still shows that label.</p> <ol> <li>Review host settings.</li> </ol> <p>In the app on the host, use <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Connections</strong> to manage connected devices. You can also choose whether to keep the computer awake, enable Computer Use, or install the Chrome extension.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Connections controls for allowing devices to control this Mac and keeping it awake.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"choose-what-to-connect\">Choose what to connect</h2> <p>Start with the laptop or desktop where you already use ChatGPT. Add an always-on computer or SSH host when you need continuous access or a different environment.</p> <h3 id=\"_1\"></h3>  <p>Your laptop or desktop</p> <p>Connect the Mac or Windows PC where the desktop app is already installed. This gives remote access to the same projects, chats, credentials, plugins, and local setup you already use.</p> <p>If that computer sleeps, loses network access, or closes the app, remote access stops until it's available again. If you use this computer as your host device, keep it plugged in and use the host's connection settings to keep it awake where available.</p> <p>On a Mac laptop, remote access can stay available with the lid open and power connected. With the lid closed, connect an external display as well. Choosing <strong>Sleep</strong> still stops remote access.</p> <p>On a Windows host, keep the session unlocked and available for tasks that use <a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a>. Computer Use on Windows runs in the foreground, so remote control is best for starting or checking work while you dedicate the host desktop to the task.</p> <h3 id=\"_2\"></h3>  <p>A dedicated always-on computer</p> <p>Use a dedicated always-on Mac or Windows PC when you want ChatGPT to stay reachable for longer-running work.</p> <p>Install the projects, credentials, MCP servers, skills, and tools ChatGPT or Codex should use on that machine.</p> <h3 id=\"_3\"></h3>  <p>A remote development environment</p> <p>Use an SSH host or managed remote development environment when the project already lives in a remote environment. Connect the desktop app host to that environment first; your phone still connects to the same host, and ChatGPT works in the remote environment with its dependencies, security policies, and compute resources.</p> <p>For SSH setup details, see <a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=connect-to-an-ssh-host\">connect to an SSH host</a>.</p> <p>For browser or desktop tasks on an always-on computer or remote host, enable Computer Use and install the Chrome extension on that host.</p> <h2 id=\"what-comes-from-the-connected-host\">What comes from the connected host</h2> <p>Your phone sends prompts, approvals, and follow-up messages to ChatGPT. The connected host provides the environment ChatGPT uses.</p> <p>That means:</p> <ul> <li>Repository files and local documents come from the connected host.</li> <li>Shell commands run on that host or remote environment.</li> <li>MCP servers, skills, browser access, and Computer Use come from that host's configuration.</li> <li>Signed-in websites and desktop apps are available only when the host can access them.</li> <li>The sandboxing settings, security controls, and action approvals still apply to the connected session.</li> </ul> <p>A secure relay layer keeps trusted machines reachable across your authorized ChatGPT devices without exposing them directly to the public internet.</p> <h2 id=\"pick-up-work-from-another-device\">Pick up work from another device</h2> <p>You can continue work from another signed-in device running the ChatGPT desktop app and supporting remote control. For example, if your laptop is unavailable, you can start a chat from your phone on an always-on host, then later open the app on your laptop and continue that same chat there.</p> <p>On a Mac or Windows device where the feature is available, use <strong>Settings &gt; Connections &gt; Control other devices</strong> to add the other host. A device can allow remote access and control another device at the same time.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Connections setup card for controlling another device from this Mac.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"connect-to-an-ssh-host\">Connect to an SSH host</h2> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, add remote projects from an SSH host and run chats against the remote filesystem and shell. Remote project chats run commands, read files, and write changes on the remote host.</p> <p>Keep the remote host configured with the same security expectations you use for normal SSH access: trusted keys, least-privilege accounts, and no unauthenticated public listeners.</p> <ol> <li>Add the host to your SSH config so Codex can discover it automatically.</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Host devbox\n     HostName devbox.example.com\n     User you\n     IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519\n</code></pre> <p>Codex reads concrete host aliases from <code>~/.ssh/config</code>, resolves them with OpenSSH, and ignores pattern-only hosts.</p> <ol> <li>Confirm you can SSH to the host from the machine running the app.</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   ssh devbox\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Install and authenticate Codex on the remote host.</li> </ol> <p>The app starts the remote Codex app server through SSH, using the remote user's login shell. Make sure the <code>codex</code> command is available on the remote host's <code>PATH</code> in that shell.</p> <ol> <li>In the app, open <strong>Settings &gt; Connections</strong>, add or enable the SSH host, then choose a remote project folder.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Connections SSH list with three remote hosts.</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"hand-off-a-thread-between-hosts\"></a> <a id=\"hand-off-a-chat-between-hosts\"></a> <a id=\"hand-off-a-task-between-hosts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"hand-off-a-chat-between-hosts\">Hand off a chat between hosts</h2> <p>Handoff moves an existing chat and its Git state between your local computer and a connected remote host. Use it to start work locally, continue in a worktree on a remote computer, and bring the chat back later.</p> <p>Before you hand off a chat, connect the destination host and save a project for the same Git repository on that host. If the project is a subdirectory of the repository, save the same subdirectory on both hosts. Codex only shows destinations with a matching saved project.</p> <p>To hand off a chat:</p> <ol> <li>Open the chat in the desktop app.</li> <li>In the chat footer, select the current run location, then select the destination host. Select <strong>This computer</strong> when handing a remote chat back to your local computer.</li> <li>Review the destination and branch, then select <strong>Hand off</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Codex creates or reuses a worktree on the destination host, transfers the chat and Git state, and switches the chat to that host. If the chat is running, handoff interrupts the current response before transferring it.</p> <p>You can also ask Codex in another chat to hand off a named chat to a connected host. Codex can't hand off the chat making the request, and handoff to a Codex cloud environment isn't supported.</p> <h2 id=\"authentication-and-network-exposure\">Authentication and network exposure</h2> <p>Remote connections use SSH to start and manage the remote Codex app server. Don't expose app-server transports directly on a shared or public network.</p> <p>If you need to reach a remote machine outside your current network, use a VPN or mesh networking tool instead of exposing the app server directly to the internet.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2> <h3 id=\"you-dont-see-the-host-on-your-phone\">You don't see the host on your phone</h3> <p>Confirm that the desktop app is running on the host, you've enabled <strong>Allow other devices to connect</strong>, and both devices use the same ChatGPT account and workspace. If you haven't used the connection since June 8, 2026, update both apps and pair the devices again.</p> <h3 id=\"remote-control-is-off-after-you-sign-back-in\">Remote Control is off after you sign back in</h3> <p>Signing out of ChatGPT turns off <strong>Remote Control</strong>, but it doesn't remove your existing device pairings. After you sign back in, turn on <strong>Remote Control</strong> to restore the previous connection state.</p> <p>If you see an error after you turn on <strong>Remote Control</strong> and select <strong>Add</strong>, restart the ChatGPT desktop app on the host, then try again.</p> <h3 id=\"the-approval-request-doesnt-appear\">The approval request doesn't appear</h3> <p>In the ChatGPT mobile app for iOS, open <strong>Codex</strong>. If your mobile app still shows <strong>Remote</strong>, open it instead. Confirm that the phone and host use the same ChatGPT account and workspace, then scan the QR code again or restart setup from the host. If you use a ChatGPT workspace, ask your admin to confirm that they've enabled Remote Control access.</p> <h3 id=\"the-remote-session-disconnects\">The remote session disconnects</h3> <p>Check whether the host went to sleep, lost network access, or closed the app. Keep the host awake and connected while ChatGPT works.</p> <h3 id=\"authentication-blocks-setup\">Authentication blocks setup</h3> <p>Complete the account or workspace authentication prompt shown during setup. If your organization requires SSO, multi-factor authentication, or a passkey, finish that flow before trying again. If setup still fails, ask your workspace admin to confirm that they've enabled Remote Control access.</p> <h2 id=\"see-also\">See also</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT desktop app</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f449586d4612e83c\">Features</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257\">ChatGPT desktop app settings</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">Chrome extension</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Command line options</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Authentication</a></li> </ul>"};
